The EUTs must cover:

- highest number of verification scale intervals, $ n_{\mathrm{max}} $;

- lowest verification scale interval, $ e_{\mathrm{min}} $;

- lowest input signal, $ \mu\mathrm{V} / e $ (when using analog strain gauge load cells);

- all accuracy classes;

- all temperature ranges;

- single range, multiple range or multi-interval instrument;

- maximum size of load receptor, if significant;

- metrologically relevant features (see 3.10.4.5);

- maximum number of instrument functions;

- maximum number of indications;

- maximum number of peripheral devices connected;

- maximum number of implemented digital devices;

- maximum number of analog and digital interfaces;

- several load receptors, if connectable to the indicator; and

- different types of power supply (mains and/or batteries).

